 2. 🤝 Trump&#x27;s Anthropic truce 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Commerce Secretary Howard Lutnick speaks at the G20 Innovation Ministerial in Chapel Hill, N.C., today. Photo: Matt Ramey/AFP via Getty Images CHAPEL HILL, N.C. — Commerce Secretary Howard Lutnick said the Trump administration trusts Anthropic again after months of clashes with the AI company.

 The statement is a remarkable turnaround from the bitter fight over national security and AI safeguards. 💡 I asked Lutnick at today's G20 innovation summit in Chapel Hill, N.C., if he trusts CEO Dario Amodei. He told me: "We trust Anthropic."

 Lutnick continued: "They've done what we asked. They're back on the right side. So the answer is: Yes." 🔎 The declaration comes as Anthropic co-founder Tom Brown takes a more prominent role in the company's relationship with the White House, including a headlining role at this week's G20 Innovation Ministerial, Axios' Maria Curi reports. 

 Industry leaders know that aligning with the Trump administration goes a long way. Brown ,  who praised Trump's pro-data-center intervention , offers a reset for a company once on the outs with the White House. Go deeper ... More from the interview . 

 
 
