 3. ⚡️ Catch me up 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The USS Abraham Lincoln approaches a port in Thailand today. Photo: Andre Malerba/Bloomberg via Getty Images ⚓ The USS Abraham Lincoln aircraft carrier docked in Thailand today after its grueling Middle East deployment sparked concerns about sailors' mental health and living conditions. Today is the first full port stop in more than nine months — a deployment Trump said last month wasn't "nearly long enough." Go deeper . ⚖️ Google secured a major court win today when a judge ruled the tech giant won't have to spin off its "network" ad business. The decision has enormous implications for the $1 trillion global advertising economy, Axios' Sara Fischer reports . 💰 The U.S. Mint began selling gold-colored $1 coins featuring an image of Trump today. The coins can be used as legal tender, but that doesn't guarantee every store will accept them, Axios' Herb Scribner reports . 🇨🇦 Trump's beef with Canada is irking Americans. More than 6 in 10 (63%) oppose Trump's executive order to rename Lake Ontario "Lake America," per a recent Reuters-Ipsos poll . Americans also expressed wariness over the renewed U.S.-Canada trade war, Axios' Avery Lotz reports . 🐅 Legendary golfer Tiger Woods will have his driver's license suspended for five years after striking a deal in his DUI case today. He was also ordered to pay $1,500 in fines. Go deeper . 
 
